          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homes a submersible sump pump is the better default: quieter, more powerful, easy to seal under a lid and available in sizes for serious water. A pedestal pump earns its place in narrow pits, unfinished basements and homes with only occasional water, where its low price, dry motor and easy servicing outweigh the noise.
          </p>
